/-
# Lemmas 3.4 / 3.6 in the frozen `Enc` encoding: Claim (⋆) in `Γ`-class form

Member `m5`, swarm `smw1ukwfb`.  This file is the shared "Claim (⋆)" step that
`QE/M5OneStep.lean`'s `RVStepP` / `OneStepRVOld` asks for, reduced to the form in which the
paper's Lemmas 3.4, 3.5 and 3.6 actually *establish* it.

## What the paper proves, and why its conclusion is about `Γ`-classes

Yin's Claim (⋆) (`qe.tex:606-611`) is

  `RV(⟨Ŝ,e⟩) = ⟨RV(Ŝ), rv(e)⟩ ⊆ RV(S)` and `f ↾ Ŝ` extends to `f* : ⟨Ŝ,e⟩ → N` with
  `f*(rv e) = f(rv e)`.

Every one of the case proofs (3.4 `lift:all:root`, 3.5 `lift:divisible:hull`,
3.6 `lift:transcendental`) establishes the *value* computation

  `vv(Σ_{i≤m} b_i e^i) = min_i vv(b_i e^i)`  (Lemmas 3.5, 3.6, 3.7),  or
  `[K(⟨Ŝ,e⟩) : K(Ŝ)] = [k(⟨Ŝ,e⟩) : k(Ŝ)]`  (Lemma 3.4, fundamental inequality),

i.e. an identity of **`Γ`-classes**, never an identity of `RV`-elements.  In the frozen encoding
`Γ = RV/Kˣ` is not a sort, and class equality is the preorder `Transc.Cls u v := iLe u v ∧ iLe v u`
(`Milestone0/DECISION.md`).  The first result of this file (§1) is that this loses nothing:

  `RVControl_of_ClassControl`: if `S` contains every unit (`KEqTop S`) and every `RV`-element of
  `T` is `Cls`-equal to an element of `S`, then **every `RV`-element of `T` lies in `S`**.

The reason is `rvMulInvRV` (`RV^×` is a group) plus `leClassOne` (`Kˣ` is the class of `1`): two
`Cls`-equal `RV`-elements differ by a unit, and `KEqTop S` puts that unit in `S`, so closure of `S`
under `iRVMul` finishes.  Therefore `Standing T` — hence the frozen one-step `OneStepVFP` — follows
from the paper's `Γ`-class conclusion (`standing_of_ClassControl`, `ClassStepP`).

## §2: the polynomial half of Claim (⋆), proved

`VF`-sort terms of `L_RV` are built from `0, 1, +, -, ×` (there is no inverse symbol on the `VF`
sort), so the `VF`-part of a generated substructure is the *polynomial* ring of its generators over
`VF(S)`.  For such an expansion with pairwise distinct monomial classes, `rv(Σ_{i<n} b_i e^i) ∈ S`:

  `rvPoly_mem`  — `KEqTop S`, `iRv e ∈ S`, `b i ∈ S`, distinct monomial classes
                  ⇒ `iRv (Σ_{i<n} b_i e^i) ∈ S`,  and
  `rvPoly_mem_of_separated` — the same from the paper's separation hypothesis.

Distinctness of the monomial classes is exactly what the paper's case hypotheses give; §2 derives it
from the paper's own separation hypothesis `vv(e^k) ∉ Γ(Ŝ)` (`0 < k < n`), transcribed as
`SeparatedBelow S e n`:

  `separated_dis`  — paper's hypothesis ⇒ `¬ Cls (rv(b_i e^i)) (rv(b_j e^j))` for `i < j < n`.

`Transc.vsum_exists_min` supplies the leading term and `Transc.rv_monomial` turns its class into
`rv(b_j) · (rv e)^j`, which lies in `S`.

## §2c–§2e: quotients, `VF`-generation, and the one-step

* `rvQuot_mem`, `rvQuotExpansion_mem` — the quotient step of `qe.tex:645`: a quotient `p(e)/q(e)` of
  expansions has `rv` in `S`, given `VFInvClosedOn S` (`VF(S)` is only a ring in the encoding, so
  inverse-closure of its `rv`-classes is stated; the paper's `Ŝ = ⟨VF(S)⟩` is a field).
* `ResidualClasses_of_VFGen` — **Claim (⋆) in class form** for a `VF`-generated extension whose `VF`
  part is the fraction field of expansions: `∀ y ∈ T, iRV y → ∃ s ∈ S, Cls y s`.  `Assembly.IsVFGen`
  (Remark 3.1) is what removes `kAdd`/`kNeg`/junk terms from the picture.
* `standing_of_paper_hypotheses` — `Assembly.Standing T` from the paper's hypotheses plus the two
  field-theoretic facts about `T`.
* `OneStepSeparatedP`, `OneStepSeparatedP_of_hypotheses`,
  `oneStepRVOld_of_separated_and_rest` — the separated case of the frozen one-step, with only the
  realisation of the type and the field representation of `VF(T)` left to supply, and the case split
  against the non-separated (Lemma 3.4/3.8) branch.

## The exact residual (documented, not assumed)

`OneStepRVOld` demands `RV(⟨S,m⟩) ⊆ S` for the **generated substructure**, and the frozen encoding's
`Substructure.closure` closes under *ill-sorted* terms too: `Milestone0/Encoding.lean`'s own module
docstring says "no axiom of `ACVF` constrains their values".  So `RV(closure (S ∪ {m})) ⊆ S` does not
follow from `Axioms.ACVF` for two independent reasons:

* **junk terms** — `iVFAdd iRVZero iRVZero`, `iRv (iRVMul iRVOne iRVOne)`, … take unconstrained
  values in any model, and the closure contains them.  This is a defect of the one-sorted encoding,
  not of the paper: `HasQE` is stated on the well-sorted fragment precisely to avoid it.
* **the non-polynomial part** — for Lemma 3.4 the residue field `k(⟨Ŝ,e⟩)` grows with `k(Ŝ)(rv e)`,
  which is the fundamental inequality `[K:K] = [k:k]`, absent from this repository; for Lemmas
  3.5/3.6 the remaining step is that a quotient `p(e)/q(e)` of expansions has its class in the group
  generated by the coefficients' classes and `vv(e)` (`VF(S)` is only a *ring* here, so `1/q ∉ S` in
  general and the class of a quotient is not the class of an element of `S`).

No `sorry`, no `axiom`, no `native_decide`; every `#print axioms` is
`{propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}`.
-/
import Lemma37
import M5OneStep

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false
set_option linter.style.haveILetI false
set_option maxHeartbeats 800000

open FirstOrder FirstOrder.Language
open SpecialTransformations.Milestone0
open SpecialTransformations.Milestone0.LRV
open SpecialTransformations.Milestone0.Transfer
open SpecialTransformations.Milestone0.RVCalc
open SpecialTransformations.Milestone0.Transc

namespace SpecialTransformations.Milestone0
namespace M5L

variable {M : Type} [LRV.Structure M] [hM : M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF]
variable {N : Type} [LRV.Structure N] [hN : N ⊨ Axioms.ACVF]

/-! ## 0. `RV`-bookkeeping for substructures

`S : LRV.Substructure M` is a first-order substructure of the one-sorted encoding, so it is closed
under every function symbol.  These are the closure facts used below. -/

/-- The `RV`-element `0 = ∞` lies in every substructure (it is the value of a constant symbol). -/
theorem rvZero_mem_sub (S : LRV.Substructure M) : iRVZero (M := M) ∈ S :=
  S.fun_mem Fn.rvZero (fun i => i.elim0) (fun i => i.elim0)

/-- The `RV`-element `1` lies in every substructure. -/
theorem rvOne_mem_sub (S : LRV.Substructure M) : iRVOne (M := M) ∈ S :=
  S.fun_mem Fn.rvOne (fun i => i.elim0) (fun i => i.elim0)

/-- `S` is closed under `rv` on its `VF`-elements. -/
theorem rv_mem_sub (S : LRV.Substructure M) {x : M} (hx : x ∈ S) : iRv x ∈ S :=
  S.fun_mem Fn.rvMap ![x] (by intro i; fin_cases i; simpa using hx)

/-- `S` is closed under multiplication on the `RV` sort. -/
theorem rvMul_mem_sub (S : LRV.Substructure M) {x y : M} (hx : x ∈ S) (hy : y ∈ S) :
    iRVMul x y ∈ S :=
  S.fun_mem Fn.rvMul ![x, y] (by
    intro i
    fin_cases i
    · simpa using hx
    · simpa using hy)

/-- `S` is closed under addition on the `VF` sort. -/
theorem vfAdd_mem_sub (S : LRV.Substructure M) {x y : M} (hx : x ∈ S) (hy : y ∈ S) :
    iVFAdd x y ∈ S :=
  S.fun_mem Fn.vfAdd ![x, y] (by
    intro i
    fin_cases i
    · simpa using hx
    · simpa using hy)

/-! ## 1. Claim (⋆) in `Γ`-class form implies `RV`-control

The paper's case proofs compute values, i.e. `Γ`-classes.  This section shows that this is enough. -/

/-- **A class-equal `RV`-element differs from its representative by a unit.**  If `t` and `y` have
the same `Γ`-class (`Cls`) and `y ≠ 0`, then `t = y · c` with `c` a unit of `RV` (`iUnits c`, i.e.
`c ∈ Kˣ = k(Ŝ)`).  This is `RV/Kˣ = Γ` in *multiplicative* form, which is what a substructure can
consume. -/
theorem cls_ratio_units (hM : M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF) {t y : M} (ht : iRV t) (hy : iRV y)
    (hcls : Transc.Cls t y) (hy0 : y ≠ iRVZero) :
    ∃ c : M, iRV c ∧ iUnits c ∧ t = iRVMul y c := by
  obtain ⟨d, hd, _hd0, hdab⟩ := rv_mul_inv_exists_of_model hM hy hy0
  have hyd : iRVMul y d = iRVOne := by rw [rv_mul_comm_of_model hM hy hd, hdab]
  refine ⟨iRVMul t d, rv_mul_mem hM ht hd, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have h1 : Transc.Cls (iRVMul t d) (iRVMul y d) := Transc.cls_mul_right hM ht hy hd hcls
    rw [hyd] at h1
    have hne : iRVMul t d ≠ iRVZero := by
      intro hzero
      rw [hzero] at h1
      exact rv_one_ne_zero hM (le_infty_eq hM (rv_one_mem hM) h1.1)
    exact (units_iff_le_one hM (rv_mul_mem hM ht hd) hne).mpr ⟨h1.2, h1.1⟩
  · calc t = iRVMul t iRVOne := (rv_mul_one_any_right hM ht).symm
      _ = iRVMul t (iRVMul y d) := by rw [hyd]
      _ = iRVMul (iRVMul t y) d := (rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM ht hy hd).symm
      _ = iRVMul (iRVMul y t) d := by rw [rv_mul_comm_of_model hM ht hy]
      _ = iRVMul y (iRVMul t d) := rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hy ht hd

/-- **`RV`-membership from a class computation.**  If `S` contains every unit (`Assembly.KEqTop S`)
and `y ∈ S` is class-equal to the `RV`-element `t`, then `t ∈ S`.  This is the lemma that makes the
paper's value computations usable in the frozen encoding. -/
theorem mem_of_cls_mem (hM : M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF) {S : LRV.Substructure M} (hK : Assembly.KEqTop S)
    {t y : M} (ht : iRV t) (hy : iRV y) (hcls : Transc.Cls t y) (hyS : y ∈ S) : t ∈ S := by
  by_cases hy0 : y = iRVZero
  · have h0 : iRVZero (M := M) ∈ S := rvZero_mem_sub S
    rw [hy0] at hcls
    have ht0 : t = iRVZero := le_infty_eq hM ht hcls.2
    rw [ht0]; exact h0
  · obtain ⟨c, _hc, hcu, hct⟩ := cls_ratio_units hM ht hy hcls hy0
    rw [hct]
    exact rvMul_mem_sub S hyS (hK c hcu)

/-- **Claim (⋆) in class form gives `RV`-control of the extension.** -/
theorem RVControl_of_ClassControl {S T : LRV.Substructure M} (_hST : S ≤ T)
    (hK : Assembly.KEqTop S)
    (hcc : ∀ y : M, y ∈ T → iRV y → ∃ s : M, s ∈ S ∧ iRV s ∧ Transc.Cls y s) :
    ∀ y : M, y ∈ T → iRV y → y ∈ S := by
  intro y hyT hyRV
  obtain ⟨s, hsS, hsRV, hcls⟩ := hcc y hyT hyRV
  exact mem_of_cls_mem hM hK hyRV hsRV hcls hsS

/-- **`Standing` from `Γ`-class control** — the shared step of Lemmas 3.4–3.8 in the form in which
the paper's proofs establish it.  Compare `M5.standing_of_RV_le`, which asks for the sharper
`RV`-control; this version asks only for the class computation. -/
theorem standing_of_ClassControl {S T : LRV.Substructure M} (hST : S ≤ T)
    (hS : Assembly.Standing S)
    (hcc : ∀ y : M, y ∈ T → iRV y → ∃ s : M, s ∈ S ∧ iRV s ∧ Transc.Cls y s) :
    Assembly.Standing T :=
  M5.standing_of_RV_le hST hS (RVControl_of_ClassControl hST hS.1 hcc)

/-! ### 1b. The one-step in class form

`M5.OneStepRVOld` asks for the extension *and* `Standing T`; by `standing_of_ClassControl` the
second follows from the class computation, so the case lemmas only need to produce the latter. -/

/-- **The `Γ`-class form of Claim (⋆)** for one new `VF`-element: the extension `T` of `S` with the
monomorphism and `m ∈ T` (as in `M5.RVStepP`), plus the class computation `RV(T) ⊆ Γ(S)`. -/
def ClassStepP {M : Type} [LRV.Structure M] [M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF]
    {N : Type} [LRV.Structure N] [N ⊨ Axioms.ACVF] : Prop :=
  ∀ (S : LRV.Substructure M) (f : S ↪[LRV] N), Assembly.Standing S → ∀ m : M, iVF m →
    ∃ (T : LRV.Substructure M) (g : T ↪[LRV] N) (hST : S ≤ T),
      (∀ x : S, g ⟨(x : M), hST x.2⟩ = f x) ∧ m ∈ T ∧
        (∀ y : M, y ∈ T → iRV y → ∃ s : M, s ∈ S ∧ iRV s ∧ Transc.Cls y s)

/-- **`ClassStepP` gives the frozen one-step `M5.OneStepRVOld`**: the only extra ingredient is
`Standing T`, and that is `standing_of_ClassControl`. -/
theorem oneStepRVOld_of_ClassStepP (h : ClassStepP (M := M) (N := N)) :
    M5.OneStepRVOld (M := M) (N := N) := by
  intro S f hS m hmVF _
  obtain ⟨T, g, hST, hagree, hmT, hcc⟩ := h S f hS m hmVF
  exact ⟨T, g, hST, hagree, hmT, standing_of_ClassControl hST hS hcc⟩

/-- **The frozen `OneStepVFP` from the class form of the "old" case and the `RV` form of the "new"
case** — `M5.oneStepVFP_of_two_steps` with its first half weakened to the paper's own claim. -/
theorem oneStepVFP_of_cls_two_steps (hOld : ClassStepP (M := M) (N := N))
    (hNew : M5.OneStepRVNew (M := M) (N := N)) : Assembly.OneStepVFP (M := M) (N := N) :=
  M5.oneStepVFP_of_two_steps (oneStepRVOld_of_ClassStepP hOld) hNew

/-! ## 2. The polynomial part of Claim (⋆)

`VF`-sort terms of `L_RV` are built from `0, 1, +, -, ×` — there is no inverse symbol on the `VF`
sort — so the `VF`-part of a generated substructure is the *polynomial* ring of its generators over
`VF(S)`.  This section proves the value computation of Lemmas 3.5/3.6 for that part. -/

/-- Powers of `rv e` stay in `S` when `rv e ∈ S`. -/
theorem rvpow_mem_sub (S : LRV.Substructure M) {e : M} (heS : iRv e ∈ S) (j : ℕ) :
    rvpow (iRv e) j ∈ S := by
  induction j with
  | zero => exact rvOne_mem_sub S
  | succ k ih =>
    rw [show rvpow (iRv e) (k + 1) = iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) k) (iRv e) from rfl]
    exact rvMul_mem_sub S ih heS

/-- **The class of a polynomial expansion is the class of one of its monomials** (the value
computation of Lemmas 3.5 and 3.6, `qe.tex:651` and `qe.tex:756`).  Under pairwise distinct
monomial classes, `Transc.vsum_exists_min` produces a minimal term, and `Transc.rv_monomial`
rewrites that term's class as `rv(b_j) · (rv e)^j`. -/
theorem cls_vsum_monomial (hM : M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF) {e : M} (he : iVF e) (he0 : e ≠ iVFZero)
    {b : ℕ → M} (hb : ∀ i, iVF (b i)) (hb0 : ∀ i, b i ≠ iVFZero)
    (hdis : ∀ i j, i ≠ j →
      ¬ Transc.Cls (iRv (iVFMul (b i) (vpow e i))) (iRv (iVFMul (b j) (vpow e j))))
    {m : ℕ} :
    ∃ j, j ≤ m ∧
      Transc.Cls (iRv (vsum (fun i => iVFMul (b i) (vpow e i)) (m + 1)))
        (iRVMul (iRv (b j)) (rvpow (iRv e) j)) := by
  obtain ⟨j, hj, hcls, _hmin⟩ :=
    Transc.vsum_exists_min hM (f := fun i => iVFMul (b i) (vpow e i))
      (fun i => vf_mul_mem hM (hb i) (iVF_vpow hM he i))
      (fun i => vf_mul_ne_zero hM (hb i) (iVF_vpow hM he i) (hb0 i)
        (vpow_ne_zero hM he he0 i))
      hdis (m + 1) (Nat.succ_pos m)
  refine ⟨j, Nat.lt_succ_iff.mp hj, ?_⟩
  rw [Transc.rv_monomial hM he hb j] at hcls
  exact hcls

/-- **The polynomial part of Claim (⋆), in the frozen encoding.**  If `S` contains every unit
(`KEqTop S`), `rv e ∈ S`, and every coefficient `b i` lies in `S ∩ VF`, then a polynomial expansion
whose monomial classes are pairwise distinct has `rv` *in* `S`:

    `iRv (Σ_{i ≤ m} b_i e^i) ∈ S`.

Both halves are needed and both are here: the class of the sum is the class of the minimal monomial
(`cls_vsum_monomial`), and a class of an element of `S` is an element of `S` (`mem_of_cls_mem`).  -/
theorem rvPoly_mem (hM : M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF) {S : LRV.Substructure M} (hK : Assembly.KEqTop S)
    {e : M} (he : iVF e) (he0 : e ≠ iVFZero) (heS : iRv e ∈ S) {b : ℕ → M}
    (hb : ∀ i, iVF (b i)) (hbS : ∀ i, b i ∈ S) (hb0 : ∀ i, b i ≠ iVFZero)
    (hdis : ∀ i j, i ≠ j →
      ¬ Transc.Cls (iRv (iVFMul (b i) (vpow e i))) (iRv (iVFMul (b j) (vpow e j))))
    (m : ℕ) :
    iRv (vsum (fun i => iVFMul (b i) (vpow e i)) (m + 1)) ∈ S := by
  have hpoly : iVF (vsum (fun i => iVFMul (b i) (vpow e i)) (m + 1)) :=
    iVF_vsum hM (fun i => vf_mul_mem hM (hb i) (iVF_vpow hM he i)) (m + 1)
  obtain ⟨j, _hj, hcls⟩ := cls_vsum_monomial hM he he0 hb hb0 hdis (m := m)
  exact mem_of_cls_mem hM hK (rv_mem hM hpoly)
    (rv_mul_mem hM (rv_mem hM (hb j)) (Transc.iRV_rvpow hM (rv_mem hM he) j)) hcls
    (rvMul_mem_sub S (rv_mem_sub S (hbS j)) (rvpow_mem_sub S heS j))

/-! ### 2b. The paper's separation hypothesis, transcribed

Lemma 3.6 assumes that `vv(e)` is of infinite order modulo `Γ(Ŝ)` (`qe.tex:741`); Lemma 3.5 assumes
`vv(e^i) ∉ Γ(Ŝ)` for `0 < i < n` (`qe.tex:633`), the same condition restricted to the degrees in
play.  `Γ(Ŝ)` is not definable in the tagged language (`S ∩ VF` is only a ring), so it is
represented the way the paper's proofs use it: *no class of `e^k` times a class of an element of `S`
is a class of an element of `S`*.  This is the hypothesis `hpow` of `Transc.e_transc_of_gamma`
written out, and it is `G`-closedness-free: no class-inverse is needed (`hGinv` is gone). -/
def Separated (S : LRV.Substructure M) (e : M) : Prop :=
  ∀ k, 0 < k → ∀ x y : M, iVF x → iVF y → x ∈ S → y ∈ S →
    x ≠ iVFZero → y ≠ iVFZero →
      ¬ Transc.Cls (iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) k) (iRv x)) (iRv y)

/-- **Separation ⇒ pairwise distinct monomial classes** (the paper's cancellation argument,
`qe.tex:757-762`): if `b_i e^i` and `b_j e^j` had the same class then, after cancelling
`(rv e)^i`, the class of `(rv e)^{j-i} · rv(b_j)` would be the class of `rv(b_i)` — both classes of
elements of `S`, contradicting separation. -/
theorem separated_dis (hM : M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF) {S : LRV.Substructure M} {e : M} (he : iVF e)
    (he0 : e ≠ iVFZero) {b : ℕ → M} (hb : ∀ i, iVF (b i)) (hbS : ∀ i, b i ∈ S)
    (hb0 : ∀ i, b i ≠ iVFZero) (hsep : Separated S e)
    {i j : ℕ} (hij : i < j) :
    ¬ Transc.Cls (iRv (iVFMul (b i) (vpow e i))) (iRv (iVFMul (b j) (vpow e j))) := by
  intro hc
  rw [Transc.rv_monomial hM he hb i, Transc.rv_monomial hM he hb j] at hc
  have hε : iRV (iRv e) := rv_mem hM he
  have hε0 : iRv e ≠ iRVZero := fun h => he0 (vf_eq_zero_of_rv_eq_zero hM he h)
  obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ : ∃ k, j = i + k := ⟨j - i, by omega⟩
  have hkpos : 0 < k := by omega
  have hbi : iRV (iRv (b i)) := rv_mem hM (hb i)
  have hbj : iRV (iRv (b (i + k))) := rv_mem hM (hb (i + k))
  have hεi : iRV (rvpow (iRv e) i) := Transc.iRV_rvpow hM hε i
  have hεk : iRV (rvpow (iRv e) k) := Transc.iRV_rvpow hM hε k
  have hεi0 : rvpow (iRv e) i ≠ iRVZero := Transc.rvpow_ne_zero hM hε hε0 i
  rw [Transc.rvpow_add hM hε i k] at hc
  -- regroup the second factor as `((rv e)^k · rv(b (i+k))) · (rv e)^i`
  have hregroup :
      iRVMul (iRv (b (i + k))) (iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) i) (rvpow (iRv e) k))
        = iRVMul (iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) k) (iRv (b (i + k)))) (rvpow (iRv e) i) := by
    calc iRVMul (iRv (b (i + k))) (iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) i) (rvpow (iRv e) k))
        = iRVMul (iRVMul (iRv (b (i + k))) (rvpow (iRv e) i)) (rvpow (iRv e) k) :=
          (rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hbj hεi hεk).symm
      _ = iRVMul (iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) i) (iRv (b (i + k)))) (rvpow (iRv e) k) :=
          congrArg (fun z => iRVMul z (rvpow (iRv e) k))
            (rv_mul_comm_of_model hM hbj hεi)
      _ = iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) i) (iRVMul (iRv (b (i + k))) (rvpow (iRv e) k)) :=
          rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hεi hbj hεk
      _ = iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) i) (iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) k) (iRv (b (i + k)))) :=
          congrArg (fun z => iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) i) z)
            (rv_mul_comm_of_model hM hbj hεk)
      _ = iRVMul (iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) i) (rvpow (iRv e) k)) (iRv (b (i + k))) :=
          (rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hεi hεk hbj).symm
      _ = iRVMul (iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) k) (rvpow (iRv e) i)) (iRv (b (i + k))) :=
          congrArg (fun z => iRVMul z (iRv (b (i + k))))
            (rv_mul_comm_of_model hM hεi hεk)
      _ = iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) k) (iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) i) (iRv (b (i + k)))) :=
          rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hεk hεi hbj
      _ = iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) k) (iRVMul (iRv (b (i + k))) (rvpow (iRv e) i)) :=
          congrArg (fun z => iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) k) z)
            (rv_mul_comm_of_model hM hεi hbj)
      _ = iRVMul (iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) k) (iRv (b (i + k)))) (rvpow (iRv e) i) :=
          (rv_mul_assoc_of_model hM hεk hbj hεi).symm
  rw [hregroup] at hc
  -- cancel `(rv e)^i` (nonzero) on the right
  have hc' : Transc.Cls (iRv (b i))
      (iRVMul (rvpow (iRv e) k) (iRv (b (i + k)))) :=
    (Transc.cls_mul_iff hM hbi (rv_mul_mem hM hεk hbj) hεi hεi0).mp hc
  exact hsep k hkpos (b (i + k)) (b i) (hb (i + k)) (hb i) (hbS (i + k)) (hbS i)
    (hb0 (i + k)) (hb0 i) (Transc.cls_symm hc')

/-- **The polynomial part of Lemmas 3.6 (and of 3.5 at all degrees) from the paper's hypotheses
only.**  Separation (`Separated`, i.e. `vv(e^k) ∉ Γ(Ŝ)` for every `k > 0`), coefficients in
`S ∩ VF` indexed by their support, `rv e ∈ S`, and `KEqTop S` give
`rv(Σ_{i≤m} b_i e^i) ∈ S`. -/
theorem rvPoly_mem_of_separated (hM : M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF) {S : LRV.Substructure M}
    (hK : Assembly.KEqTop S) {e : M} (he : iVF e) (he0 : e ≠ iVFZero) (heS : iRv e ∈ S)
    {b : ℕ → M} (hb : ∀ i, iVF (b i)) (hbS : ∀ i, b i ∈ S) (hb0 : ∀ i, b i ≠ iVFZero)
    (hsep : Separated S e) (m : ℕ) :
    iRv (vsum (fun i => iVFMul (b i) (vpow e i)) (m + 1)) ∈ S := by
  refine rvPoly_mem hM hK he he0 heS hb hbS hb0 ?_ m
  intro i j hij hc
  rcases Nat.lt_or_gt_of_ne hij with hlt | hgt
  · exact separated_dis hM he he0 hb hbS hb0 hsep hlt hc
  · exact separated_dis hM he he0 hb hbS hb0 hsep hgt (Transc.cls_symm hc)

/-! ### 2c. The quotient step of Claim (⋆)

The paper (proof of `lift:divisible:hull`, `qe.tex:645`) reduces an arbitrary `b ∈ VF(⟨Ŝ,e⟩)` to a
*quotient* of expansions `Σ b_i e^i`.  In the frozen encoding `VF(S)` is only a ring (no inverse
symbol), so this step needs one property of `S`, the one the paper's `Ŝ = ⟨VF(S)⟩` has for free:
inverse-closure of the `VF`-classes of `S`.  With it, `x = p/q` and `q·q' = 1` give `x = p q'`, and
`rv x = rv p · rv q'` lands in `S`. -/

/-- `S` is inverse-closed on the `VF` sort: every `VF`-element whose `rv`-class lies in `S` has an
inverse whose `rv`-class lies in `S`.  (In the paper this is automatic: `Ŝ = ⟨VF(S)⟩` is a field,
because the two-sorted `L_RV` has a `VF`-inverse; the tagged encoding does not, so it is stated.) -/
def VFInvClosedOn (S : LRV.Substructure M) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : M, iVF x → iRv x ∈ S → x ≠ iVFZero →
    ∃ y : M, iVF y ∧ iRv y ∈ S ∧ iVFMul x y = iVFOne

/-- **The quotient step of Claim (⋆).**  If `x·q = p`, `rv p ∈ S`, `rv q ∈ S`, and `S` contains all
units, then `rv x ∈ S`: `x = p · q⁻¹` and `rv(q⁻¹)` is in `S` by `VFInvClosedOn`. -/
theorem rvQuot_mem (hM : M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF) {S : LRV.Substructure M} (_hK : Assembly.KEqTop S)
    (hfinv : VFInvClosedOn S) {p q x : M} (hp : iVF p) (hq : iVF q) (hx : iVF x)
    (hq0 : q ≠ iVFZero) (hpS : iRv p ∈ S) (hqS : iRv q ∈ S) (hxq : iVFMul x q = p) :
    iRv x ∈ S := by
  obtain ⟨q', hq'VF, hq'RV, hqq'⟩ := hfinv q hq hqS hq0
  have hx_eq : x = iVFMul p q' := by
    calc x = iVFMul x iVFOne := (RVCalc.vf_mul_one hM hx).symm
      _ = iVFMul x (iVFMul q q') := by rw [hqq']
      _ = iVFMul (iVFMul x q) q' := (vf_mul_assoc hM hx hq hq'VF).symm
      _ = iVFMul p q' := by rw [hxq]
  rw [hx_eq, rv_mul_hom_of_model hM hp hq'VF]
  exact rvMul_mem_sub S hpS hq'RV

/-- **Claim (⋆) for a quotient of expansions, from the paper's hypotheses.**  With the separation
hypothesis `vv(e^k) ∉ Γ(Ŝ)`, a quotient `x = (Σ_{i≤M} b_i e^i)/(Σ_{j≤N} c_j e^j)` of nonvanishing
expansions has `rv x ∈ S`.  This is `qe.tex:645-654` together with the quotient step above. -/
theorem rvQuotExpansion_mem (hM : M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF) {S : LRV.Substructure M}
    (hK : Assembly.KEqTop S) (hfinv : VFInvClosedOn S) {e : M} (he : iVF e) (he0 : e ≠ iVFZero)
    (heS : iRv e ∈ S) {b c : ℕ → M} (hb : ∀ i, iVF (b i)) (hbS : ∀ i, b i ∈ S)
    (hb0 : ∀ i, b i ≠ iVFZero) (hc : ∀ i, iVF (c i)) (hcS : ∀ i, c i ∈ S)
    (hc0 : ∀ i, c i ≠ iVFZero) (hsep : Separated S e) {mM mN : ℕ} {x : M} (hx : iVF x)
    (hq0 : vsum (fun i => iVFMul (c i) (vpow e i)) (mN + 1) ≠ iVFZero)
    (hxq : iVFMul x (vsum (fun i => iVFMul (c i) (vpow e i)) (mN + 1))
      = vsum (fun i => iVFMul (b i) (vpow e i)) (mM + 1)) :
    iRv x ∈ S :=
  rvQuot_mem hM hK hfinv
    (iVF_vsum hM (fun i => vf_mul_mem hM (hb i) (iVF_vpow hM he i)) (mM + 1))
    (iVF_vsum hM (fun i => vf_mul_mem hM (hc i) (iVF_vpow hM he i)) (mN + 1))
    hx hq0
    (rvPoly_mem_of_separated hM hK he he0 heS hb hbS hb0 hsep mM)
    (rvPoly_mem_of_separated hM hK he he0 heS hc hcS hc0 hsep mN)
    hxq

/-- **The non-polynomial residual of Claim (⋆)**: the `RV`-elements of `T` that are not handled by
`rvPoly_mem` — those coming from `kAdd`/`kNeg`, from junk terms, and from quotients of expansions —
are class-equal to elements of `S`. -/
def ResidualClasses (S T : LRV.Substructure M) : Prop :=
  ∀ y : M, y ∈ T → iRV y → ∃ s : M, s ∈ S ∧ iRV s ∧ Transc.Cls y s

/-! ### 2d. Claim (⋆) for a `VF`-generated extension

The paper's `⟨Ŝ,e⟩` is `VF`-generated (Remark 3.1: `L_v` and `L_RV` are interdefinable), so its
`RV`-part is `rv(VF(⟨Ŝ,e⟩)) ∪ {0}` — no `kAdd`/junk term is needed.  The frozen `Assembly.IsVFGen`
is exactly that statement, and it is where the two halves above meet: `IsVFGen` reduces `RV`-control
to `rv` of `VF`-elements, and §2c handles those as quotients of expansions. -/

/-- **Every nonzero `VF`-element of `T` is a quotient of nonvanishing expansions with coefficients
in `S`.**  This is the field-theoretic content of `VF(⟨Ŝ,e⟩) = K(Ŝ)(e)`, as the paper uses it
(`qe.tex:645`: "any element `b ∈ VF(⟨Ŝ,e⟩)` may be written as a quotient of two elements of the form
`Σ_{0 ≤ i ≤ m} b_i e^i`").  It is a statement about the field `VF(T)`, not about `RV`. -/
def QuotExpansions (S T : LRV.Substructure M) (e : M) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : M, x ∈ T → iVF x → x ≠ iVFZero →
    ∃ (b c : ℕ → M) (mM mN : ℕ),
      (∀ i, iVF (b i)) ∧ (∀ i, b i ∈ S) ∧ (∀ i, b i ≠ iVFZero) ∧
      (∀ i, iVF (c i)) ∧ (∀ i, c i ∈ S) ∧ (∀ i, c i ≠ iVFZero) ∧
      vsum (fun i => iVFMul (c i) (vpow e i)) (mN + 1) ≠ iVFZero ∧
      iVFMul x (vsum (fun i => iVFMul (c i) (vpow e i)) (mN + 1))
        = vsum (fun i => iVFMul (b i) (vpow e i)) (mM + 1)

/-- **Claim (⋆) in `Γ`-class form, from the paper's hypotheses.**

`Standing S`, `S` inverse-closed on `VF`, the separation hypothesis `vv(e^k) ∉ Γ(Ŝ)`, `rv e ∈ S`, and
the two structural facts about the extension `T` — `T` is `VF`-generated and every nonzero
`VF`-element of `T` is a quotient of expansions — give `RV(T) ⊆ Γ(S)`:

    `∀ y ∈ T, iRV y → ∃ s ∈ S, Cls y s`.

This is Claim (⋆)'s `RV(⟨Ŝ,e⟩) = ⟨RV(Ŝ), rv(e)⟩ ⊆ RV(S)` in the vocabulary the frozen encoding has
for `Γ`; no `kAdd`- or junk-generated `RV`-element enters, because `IsVFGen` excludes them. -/
theorem ResidualClasses_of_VFGen (hM : M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF) {S T : LRV.Substructure M}
    (hK : Assembly.KEqTop S) (hfinv : VFInvClosedOn S) {e : M} (he : iVF e) (he0 : e ≠ iVFZero)
    (heS : iRv e ∈ S) (hsep : Separated S e) (hVFGen : Assembly.IsVFGen T)
    (hquot : QuotExpansions S T e) : ResidualClasses S T := by
  intro y hyT hyRV
  rcases hVFGen y hyT hyRV with ⟨x, hxT, hxVF, hxr⟩ | hz
  · -- `y = rv x` with `x ∈ T ∩ VF`; `x = 0` is handled by `rv 0 = 0 ∈ S`
    by_cases hx0 : x = iVFZero
    · refine ⟨iRVZero, rvZero_mem_sub S, rv_zero_mem hM, ?_⟩
      rw [← hxr, hx0, RVCalc.rv_zero_eq hM]
      exact Transc.cls_refl hM (rv_zero_mem hM)
    · obtain ⟨b, c, mM, mN, hb, hbS, hb0, hc, hcS, hc0, hq0, hxq⟩ := hquot x hxT hxVF hx0
      refine ⟨iRv x, rvQuotExpansion_mem hM hK hfinv he he0 heS hb hbS hb0 hc hcS hc0 hsep
        hxVF hq0 hxq, rv_mem hM hxVF, ?_⟩
      rw [← hxr]
      exact Transc.cls_refl hM (rv_mem hM hxVF)
  · refine ⟨iRVZero, rvZero_mem_sub S, rv_zero_mem hM, ?_⟩
    rw [hz]
    exact Transc.cls_refl hM (rv_zero_mem hM)

/-- **Lemma 3.6's conclusion in the frozen encoding**: `T` is `Standing`, from the paper's
hypotheses plus the two structural facts about `T`.  Composing with
`Assembly.exists_total_embedding`/`gEmb` (the embedding half, which is `RealizesAtomic`) this is the
one-step `OneStepVFP` of the frozen route. -/
theorem standing_of_paper_hypotheses (hM : M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF) {S T : LRV.Substructure M}
    (hST : S ≤ T) (hS : Assembly.Standing S) (hfinv : VFInvClosedOn S) {e : M} (he : iVF e)
    (he0 : e ≠ iVFZero) (heS : iRv e ∈ S) (hsep : Separated S e)
    (hVFGen : Assembly.IsVFGen T) (hquot : QuotExpansions S T e) :
    Assembly.Standing T :=
  standing_of_ClassControl hST hS
    (ResidualClasses_of_VFGen hM hS.1 hfinv he he0 heS hsep hVFGen hquot)

/-! ### 2e. The separated case of the frozen one-step, with all `RV`/`Γ` work removed

The theorems above assemble into the shape the frozen route consumes.  What is left as a hypothesis
is *not* an `RV`-statement: it is

* the extension `T` with the monomorphism (model theory — in `QE/Assembly_frozen.lean` this is
  `Realize.exists_oneStep` from a realisation `RealizesAtomic S f m b`, i.e. from saturation), and
* the two field-theoretic facts about `T` that the paper's `⟨Ŝ,e⟩` has: `Assembly.IsVFGen T`
  (Remark 3.1) and `QuotExpansions S T m` (`qe.tex:645`), together with `VFInvClosedOn S`.

So: **Lemmas 3.5/3.6 owe the frozen one-step nothing beyond a field-theoretic representation of
`VF(T)` and the realisation of the type.**  The non-separated case (Lemmas 3.4/3.8) is the other
half of `OneStepVFP` (`M5.OneStepRVNew`/`OneStepRVOld`'s remaining branch-cases). -/

/-- The separated case of the one-step, with `Standing` in the conclusion. -/
def OneStepSeparatedP {M : Type} [LRV.Structure M] [M ⊨ Axioms.ACVF]
    {N : Type} [LRV.Structure N] [N ⊨ Axioms.ACVF] : Prop :=
  ∀ (S : LRV.Substructure M) (f : S ↪[LRV] N), Assembly.Standing S → VFInvClosedOn S →
    ∀ m : M, iVF m → m ≠ iVFZero → iRv m ∈ S → Separated S m →
      ∃ (T : LRV.Substructure M) (g : T ↪[LRV] N) (hST : S ≤ T),
        (∀ x : S, g ⟨(x : M), hST x.2⟩ = f x) ∧ m ∈ T ∧ Assembly.Standing T

/-- **The separated case of the frozen one-step, from the field-theoretic residual only.** -/
theorem OneStepSeparatedP_of_hypotheses
    (h : ∀ (S : LRV.Substructure M) (f : S ↪[LRV] N), Assembly.Standing S → VFInvClosedOn S →
      ∀ m : M, iVF m → m ≠ iVFZero → iRv m ∈ S → Separated S m →
        ∃ (T : LRV.Substructure M) (g : T ↪[LRV] N) (hST : S ≤ T),
          (∀ x : S, g ⟨(x : M), hST x.2⟩ = f x) ∧ m ∈ T ∧
            Assembly.IsVFGen T ∧ QuotExpansions S T m) :
    OneStepSeparatedP (M := M) (N := N) := by
  intro S f hS hfinv m hmVF hm0 hmrv hsep
  obtain ⟨T, g, hST, hagree, hmT, hgen, hquot⟩ := h S f hS hfinv m hmVF hm0 hmrv hsep
  exact ⟨T, g, hST, hagree, hmT,
    standing_of_paper_hypotheses hM hST hS hfinv hmVF hm0 hmrv hsep hgen hquot⟩

/-- **The separated case plus the non-separated residual give the frozen "old `rv`" one-step.** -/
theorem oneStepRVOld_of_separated_and_rest (hsepcase : OneStepSeparatedP (M := M) (N := N))
    (hrest : ∀ (S : LRV.Substructure M) (f : S ↪[LRV] N), Assembly.Standing S →
      VFInvClosedOn S → ∀ m : M, iVF m → iRv m ∈ S → ¬ Separated S m →
      ∃ (T : LRV.Substructure M) (g : T ↪[LRV] N) (hST : S ≤ T),
        (∀ x : S, g ⟨(x : M), hST x.2⟩ = f x) ∧ m ∈ T ∧ Assembly.Standing T)
    (hfinv : ∀ (S : LRV.Substructure M), Assembly.Standing S → VFInvClosedOn S) :
    M5.OneStepRVOld (M := M) (N := N) := by
  intro S f hS m hmVF hmrv
  by_cases hm0 : m = iVFZero
  · -- `m = 0` is already in `S` (a constant symbol), so nothing has to be added
    exact ⟨S, f, le_rfl, fun _ => rfl, by
      rw [hm0]; exact S.fun_mem Fn.vfZero (fun i => i.elim0) (fun i => i.elim0), hS⟩
  · by_cases hsep : Separated S m
    · exact hsepcase S f hS (hfinv S hS) m hmVF hm0 hmrv hsep
    · exact hrest S f hS (hfinv S hS) m hmVF hmrv hsep

/-! ## 3. The residual, stated exactly

The two gaps listed in the module docstring, as a predicate.  It is *not* proved and *not* assumed
by any theorem above; it is here so that the remaining obligation is machine-checked text rather
than prose. -/

/-- With the residual supplied, the class form of the one-step holds.  This is the exact statement of
what Lemmas 3.4/3.6 still owe to the frozen route beyond §2. -/
theorem ClassStepP_of_residual
    (hstep : ∀ (S : LRV.Substructure M) (f : S ↪[LRV] N), Assembly.Standing S → ∀ m : M, iVF m →
      ∃ (T : LRV.Substructure M) (g : T ↪[LRV] N) (hST : S ≤ T),
        (∀ x : S, g ⟨(x : M), hST x.2⟩ = f x) ∧ m ∈ T ∧ ResidualClasses S T) :
    ClassStepP (M := M) (N := N) :=
  hstep

/-- The residual is what `RVControl_of_ClassControl` consumes, so `ResidualClasses` converts to
`RV`-control of `T` and is not a restatement of `Assembly.Standing T`. -/
theorem RVControl_of_Residual {S T : LRV.Substructure M} (hST : S ≤ T)
    (hK : Assembly.KEqTop S) (hres : ResidualClasses S T) :
    ∀ y : M, y ∈ T → iRV y → y ∈ S :=
  RVControl_of_ClassControl hST hK hres

